 the comparison needs a tokenizer that distinguishes numeric and alphanumeric identifiers. Sort a list of versions: convert each to a tuple of ints and sort (padding is unnecessary for sorting only if you strip trailing zeros). Very long revisions that overflow a 32-bit int: compare lengths after stripping zeros, then compare lexicographically.","complexity":{"time":"O(n + m)","space":"O(n + m) (O(1) with the two-pointer variant)"},"similar":["string-to-integer-atoi","simplify-path"],"number":188,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def compareVersion(self, version1: str, version2: str) -> int:\n        pass\n"}